#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""HXC AI Mathematics Inventor — one-cell Google Colab runner.

Paste this entire file into one Google Colab cell, or upload it and run:

    %run /content/HXC_AI_MATHEMATICS_INVENTOR_COLAB.py

The program is an autonomous symbolic mathematics inventor over a
user-extensible finite grammar. It:

1. searches a space of candidate binary operations;
2. discovers a novel algebraic law;
3. searches for a compatible unary symmetry;
4. generates conjectures from observed structure;
5. rejects false conjectures with counterexamples;
6. emits a proof-carrying Lean 4 development;
7. asks the Lean kernel to verify every surviving claim.

It does not claim to generate literally every possible branch of mathematics.
"Arbitrary" here means open-ended mathematics inside an extensible typed
operator grammar whose generated claims must survive formal verification.
"""

